<title>USA: Inhale, Centeon to collaborate on drug.</title>
<headline>Inhale, Centeon to collaborate on drug.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inhale Therapeutic Systems and Centeon LLC said they entered into a collaboration to develop a pulmonary formulation of alpha-1 proteinase inhibitor to treat patients with alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, a genetic disorder that can lead to emphysema.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Centeon will receive commercialization rights worldwide outside of Japan and Inhale will receive royalties on product sales, an up-front signing fee and up to $15 million in R&amp;D funding and milestone payments.</p>
</text>
